Errors Solved:

Java Library Error

Copylibjli.so: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory

Issue: Java Runtime Environment library paths not properly set
Solution: Set up proper environment variables (PATH and LD_LIBRARY_PATH)


Chromosome ID Mismatch

CopyNo VCF records found

Issue: Reference used "chr1" format while input used "1" format
Solution: Created script to convert chromosome names consistently


Tabix Indexing Error

Copy[E::hts_idx_push] Chromosome blocks not continuous

Issue: VCF wasn't properly sorted
Solution: Added sorting by chromosome and position before indexing


Unchecked Contig Error

CopyContig 'chrmY' is not defined in the header

Issue: Chromosomes in data weren't defined in VCF header
Solution: Added proper contig definitions to header

Tips for VCF Processing with Beagle:

VCF File Requirements:

Must be sorted by chromosome and position
Must be compressed (.gz format)
Must have tabix index (.tbi file)
Chromosome names must match between input and reference


File Preparation Checklist:
Copy✓ Check chromosome naming convention
✓ Ensure header contains all contigs
✓ Sort VCF by chromosome and position
✓ Compress with bgzip
✓ Index with tabix

Tool Dependencies:
CopyRequired tools:
- bgzip (for compression)
- tabix (for indexing)
- java (for Beagle)

Processing Order:
Copy1. Convert chromosome names
2. Fix header
3. Sort data
4. Compress
5. Index

Best Practices:

Always check chromosome naming in reference files first
Validate VCF format before processing
Keep both uncompressed and compressed versions for debugging
Verify file sorting before indexing
Ensure all tools are in PATH
Monitor memory usage with large VCF files


Common Gotchas:

Double chromosome prefixes (e.g., 'chrchr1')
Missing contig definitions in header
Unsorted positions within chromosomes
Non-gzipped files with .gz extension
Missing environment variables